              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "1. A woman with suspected ruptured ectopic pregnancy has a BP of 78/46 mmHg. What is the priority?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Wait for the β-hCG result",
                    "Start methotrexate",
                    "Resuscitate immediately and arrange urgent operative management",
                    "Perform a lengthy pelvic examination first"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "2. Why may the initial haemoglobin be normal despite major acute blood loss?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Ectopic pregnancy does not cause anaemia",
                    "The concentration may not fall immediately after acute whole-blood loss",
                    "Haemoglobin is always elevated in pregnancy",
                    "The blood is confined to the uterus"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "3. Which treatment is inappropriate for a ruptured ectopic pregnancy with haemorrhagic shock?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Urgent senior review",
                    "Blood-product resuscitation",
                    "Emergency surgery",
                    "Methotrexate as definitive emergency treatment"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "4. After salpingotomy, what follow-up is especially important?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Serial β-hCG until resolution",
                    "No follow-up if pain resolves",
                    "Routine CT scanning for every patient",
                    "Daily methotrexate for all patients"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
